#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""vault: client for the owner's privacy vault (container claude-vault on Unraid, http://claude-vault:8300).

The vault holds the raw private data and its credentials (Telegram archive + session, paperless/Firefly tokens, the
local LLM); this box only gets policy-filtered results (regex net -> local LLM anonymizer -> regex net).
Raw text needs the owner's OK: the vault's own bot texts him the request with ✅ Allow once / ❌ Deny buttons (I can
never approve; fallback while that bot can't poll: a 6-digit code in the message). New incoming Telegram messages
and Gmail mails are triaged + anonymized in the vault into an event feed (`vault events`; ~/bin/vault-events turns it
into inbox notes). Gmail is READ-ONLY in the vault (IMAP EXAMINE + BODY.PEEK only: never marks, moves, deletes, sends).

  vault status [--json]                        state of the vault, LLM, Telegram login/sync, sources (no data)
  vault tg COMMAND ...                          tgread through the vault (same options; ~/bin/tgread wraps this):
        search QUERY | recent | unread-summary-data | summarize | window (counts per chat/day, no text) | chats |
        status | exclude | purge | sync |
        wipe | allowlist | set-credentials (stdin) | login-qr [--out PNG] [--timeout S] [--password-stdin] |
        login-status | login-cancel | 2fa (password on stdin) | download --chat X --msg N --reason R |
        alias set CHAT NAME [--tag T] | alias rm NAME | alias list | find-chat QUERY [--since 365d] [-n 10] |
        who NAME | media --chat X (= vault media list tg X)      chat directory: metadata only, no LLM
  vault paperless get ID [--content --reason R]   a card (metadata, amount, due date), never content; --content asks
        the owner (✅) for the anonymized text
  vault paperless fields ID [--fields a,b] [--reason R]   tier 1 free; tier-2 fields (IBAN, reference, numbers,
        addresses, dates) come back null + _withheld unless --reason asks the owner (✅)
  vault paperless suggest ID   type/correspondent/tags from the existing names, read inside the vault
  vault paperless rule test tag|type|correspondent --regex R|--any W|--all W|--literal T|--fuzzy T [--case-sensitive]
        [--name N] [--json]   which documents a rule would hit (ids + current values only)
  vault paperless search|recent|get|meta|fields|upload|task|download ...   (~/bin/paperless delegates here when
        VAULT_MODE is on; get = anonymized content; fields = whitelisted raw admin fields as JSON)
  vault paperless set ID [--title T] [--created D] [--type T] [--correspondent C] [--tag +ADD|-REMOVE] [--create]
  vault paperless rule set tag|type|correspondent NAME --regex R|--any W|--all W|--literal T|--fuzzy T|--auto|--none
        [--case-sensitive] [--inbox|--no-inbox] [--create]   |   vault paperless rules [KIND]   (metadata writes only)
  vault firefly status | summary START END | merchants START END [--limit N] | sync-status
  vault firefly check | rules | rules-set [--request-id ID --code C] < rules.json | rules-replace --reason TEXT
                                 the sync's private rules (write-only: counts + sha256 back) and a numbers-only dry run
  vault ha inventory [--json]        the owner's phone entities in Home Assistant, metadata only (kinds, no values)
  vault ha now [--json]              his current coarse flags from the vault's HA feed: zone name or away + distance
        band (+ town), drive, activity, Bluetooth categories, Wi-Fi class, sleep, alarm, battery; + their age
  vault people [--active 90d] [--relation R|set|unset] [-n 20] [--json]   person cards, fields only:
        his Telegram DM contacts with >= 10 messages in 12 months, at most 20 shown: first name (or his chat alias),
        key, relation (only he sets it), last contact dates, 30-day counts; never message text
  vault people show NAME|KEY [--json] | relation NAME [VALUE] | forget NAME | unforget NAME|KEY | rebuild
        relation NAME: the vault bot asks him (buttons, <= 20 a day); relation NAME VALUE: only when he told me (the
        vault bot confirms it to him with Undo); both need VAULT_PEOPLE_ASK=1. forget/unforget only on his request
        With VAULT_PEOPLE_ASKS=1 cards add open asks (dir from_them|from_owner, wants, urgency, due, since, status
        open|replied, refs; expire after 21 days or due + 7) and top topics of 90 days (enums); `--asks` lists only
        cards with open asks
  vault people refresh asks [--sample N] | topics     feed asks + statuses now (numbers); --sample N (<= 30): a dry
        run of the nightly triage of his own DM messages over his newest ones (counts only, nothing stored)
  vault people calibrate [--sample N] [--dry] [--force]   topic calibration in the vault (async job; Gemma labels
        chunks inside, only accuracy numbers come back); runs by itself at night; by day only --dry with --sample <= 40
  vault gmail status [--json] | search QUERY [-n N] [--folder F] [--account L|all] [--json]
        | get REF [--chars N] [--account L] [--json]
        | to-paperless REF [N] [--account L] [--title T] [--tag T] [--correspondent C] [--type T] [--created D]
  vault gmail import scan [--account L ...] [--since YYYY-MM-DD] [--max N] [--no-download] [--no-llm] [--resume ID]
        | import status [ID] [--json] | import --plan ID --categories a,b [--limit N] [--office] [--likely]
        [--pause S] [--dry-run] | import cancel [ID] | import drop ID   mail backfill into paperless, all in the
        vault: the plan rows stay there; I get counts, categories, years, sender domains / first names
        [--create] | config [--account L] [--folders A,B] [--owner-name NAME]
        Several accounts: each has a label (main = the first; `vault gmail status` lists them). REF = main:1234 or
        work:1234@Folder (from events/search: it carries the account; a bare 1234 only while there is one account).
        search: all accounts unless --account; N = the attachment number (default 1); Gmail's search syntax
        (from:x has:attachment newer_than:7d ...)
  vault llm-run -- [llm-local options] < text  llm-local in the vault on my own text (llm-local backend "vault")
  vault media list tg CHAT | gmail REF | paperless ID [--type pdf|photo|voice|video|audio|document] [--since 30d]
        [--grep WORD] [-n N] [--json]      files as metadata only (names privacy-filtered), numbered, with keys
  vault media request KEY... | --pick 1,3  --reason R [--keep 2h] [--no-wait]   up to 5 files; the owner gets
        ✅ Allow once / 📋 Facts only (PDF/.ics) / ❌ Deny; files land in ~/.cache/vault/media/<rid>/ (0700/0600) and
        are deleted after --keep (2 h by default and at most) by `vault media gc` (cron */5 + every call)
  vault media release RID [--wait N] | facts KEY|N [--kind travel|event|booking|ics|generic] (no approval: fields
        from the anonymized text; never PNR, ticket numbers, prices) | gc [--quiet] | status
  vault raw request --source tg|tg-file|paperless|paperless-file|firefly|gmail|test --reason R [--query JSON] [...]
        (gmail: --uid REF [--account L] [--attachment N | --eml]: the mail as text, one attachment, or the .eml)
  vault raw release REQUEST_ID [CODE] [--out PATH] [--wait S | --no-wait]   (CODE only for a fallback-code request;
        without it: waits up to --wait s, default 100, for his tap, then exit 10 = still pending)  |  vault raw pending
  vault facts tg CHAT [--since 60d] [-n 400] | gmail REF [--account L] [--chars N]  [--brief]   events, to-dos,
        places, decisions, open questions as JSON: read from the anonymized (not paraphrased) text in the
        vault, every value found in it, dates worked out from the message times; long windows: vault --async facts ...
  vault ask tg (--chat C | --search Q) [--since 30d] [--kind K] ["question"] [--json]   an ANSWER, not text
        kinds yesno, when, who, deadline, actionable, requests, count, short, interests, digest; values
        checked in the vault. `vault ask gmail REF [--kind K] ["question"]` (default: the mail card). = `tgread ask`.
        --retrieval hybrid|keyword: hybrid = keyword hits + the question's semantic neighbours from the
        vault's index, fused into conversation chunks (one answer part; --chars 500-4500, default 2000); a long --chat
        window reads only the best-matching chunks for question kinds. Default: VAULT_INDEX (keyword when off); falls
        back to keyword per call when the index can't serve (answer `retrieval`: mode, counts, fallback reason)
  --text --reason "why" on tg search|recent|unread-summary-data|summarize, gmail search|get, find: the TEXT, only
        after the owner's ✅ in the vault bot (exit 10 + how to pick it up); --no-text: the default (hits,
        digest, cards; TEXT_DEFAULT = False in the vault).
  vault find "QUERY" [--since 30d] [--sources tg,gmail,paperless] [-n 15] [--json]   one ranked list across Telegram,
        Gmail and paperless with Swiss German / German / English variants (Hochzeit = Hochziit =
        wedding, Freitag = Fritig, JGA = Junggesellenabschied, Geburtstag = Geburi), ue = ü, word starts; one
        anonymize call; paperless as metadata only.  `vault tg search QUERY --expand` = the same variants in Telegram
  vault plans [--days 14] [--json]       dated facts of the event feed (calendar suggestions):
        "Sat 17.10 16:00 Concert, Town Hall · Choir"; then the calendar rule (add obvious ones, ask if unsure)
  vault events [--since CURSOR|latest] [--max N] [--source telegram|gmail] [--json]    (alias: vault tg events)
  vault events rules | mute|priority|normal [--source S] --chat KEY|--sender KEY   (per source + chat/sender;
        gmail: --chat DOMAIN (subdomains too) | --sender ADDRESS or its pseudonym)
  vault audit [--days 7] [--json]  |  vault alerts [--to-inbox]  |  vault metrics [--days 1] [--json]  (health numbers)
  vault --async tg search|recent|unread-summary-data|summarize ... | gmail search|get ... | paperless get ... |
        media facts ... | llm-run ...      (--async anywhere before `--`): runs it as a job in the vault, prints its
        id at once (tg summarize then goes per chat/day + one merge, with progress and part results)
  vault job wait ID [--max 230] [--partial] [--json]   the job's answer, printed like the command would (its exit
        code); still running after --max s: exit 12 (progress on stderr; --partial: the parts done so far)
  vault job list [--json]  |  vault job cancel ID       (results are kept 30 min; a vault restart drops every job)
  vault secret list | set NAME [--request-id ID [--code CODE]] (JSON on stdin) | rotate NAME --reason R
  vault index status [--full] [--json]   embedding server (VAULT_EMBED, idle CPU priority), sqlite-vec,
        the index (chunks, chats, size, lag, build progress) and the last bake-off (recall, MRR: numbers only)
  vault index rebuild [--reconcile]   queue a full shadow rebuild (or a reconcile) for the vault's index thread
  vault index eval [--sample 2000] [--queries 400] [--models a,b] [--seed N]   the bake-off inside the vault, as an
        async job at background priority (~1-2 h; Gemma writes the questions); then `vault index status --full`
  vault deploy request [COMMIT] [--wait S]   a Telegram-approved vault deploy: the owner's server (deploy runner)
        reviews COMMIT (default HEAD of ~/opt/claude-vault; it must be on GitHub main: vault admin deploy pushes), the
        vault bot sends him a card with the server's facts and ✅ Deploy / ❌ Cancel, the server deploys on ✅. Changes
        to docker-compose.yml (container privileges) and first deploys need his User Scripts button.
        Exit 0 deployed, 10 still under way (reviewing / his decision / deploying), 1 not deployed
  vault deploy status [ID] [--wait S] [--json]   the runner (alive, deployed commit) and the deploy requests
  vault admin deploy | logs [-n N] | ps   deploy: push the source to GitHub (vault-git-sync) and print "ready for your
        deploy: <commit>", the commits since his last deploy and flagged files; logs/ps: the read-only verbs
        vault-logs/vault-ps. The owner deploys (vault deploy request, or his User Scripts button).
  vault admin init | test | restart | down | test-instance | env-add   the owner's, refused here: the API token's
        hash (vault-deploy token-hash), the image tests (every deploy runs them), restart/stop (the Docker tab), the
        server's .env values (by hand). They run only where `unraid-ssh mode` reports root (no lockdown).
Global: --instance test (the ephemeral test vault: http://claude-vault-test:8300, ~/.secrets/vault-test-token).
Config: ~/.config/vault/url, ~/.secrets/vault-token (0600), ~/.config/vault/mode (on = paperless via the vault).
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 vault/LLM/source unavailable or not configured, 10 waiting for the owner
(his tap or code), 12 job still running (vault job wait), 75 busy/try later, 77 auth; tg and llm-run pass through
tgread's and llm-local's own exit codes.
"""
